 class=\"oeuv\">Ran.</span>\n<span class=\"refch\">336, 337</span> ||</div>\n<div class=\"pp\"><span class=\"ppa\">3</span> juste, honnête,\n<span class=\"ital\">p. opp. à</span> <span class=\"grec\">ἐπίορκος,</span> <span class=\"aut\">Xén.</span> <span class=\"oeuv\">An.</span> <span class=\"refch\">2, 6, 25 ;</span>\n<span class=\"ital\">joint à</span> <span class=\"grec\">δίκαιος,</span> <span class=\"aut\">Plat.</span> <span class=\"oeuv\">Rsp.</span> <span class=\"refpa\">615</span><span class=\"refpb\">b</span> ; <span class=\"grec\">ὅσιος εἴς τινα,</span>\n<span class=\"aut\">Eur.</span> <span class=\"oeuv\">Her.</span>\n<span class=\"refch\">719 ;</span> <span class=\"grec\">περί\nτινα,</span> <span class=\"aut\">Eur.</span> <span class=\"oeuv\">Cycl.</span> <span class=\"refch\">125,</span> respectueux\nenvers qqn ; <span class=\"ital\">avec le gén.</span> <span class=\"grec\">ἱερῶν πατρῴων ὅσιος,</span> <span class=\"aut\">Eschl.</span>\n<span class=\"oeuv\">Sept.</span> <span class=\"refch\">1010,</span>\nqui tient en honneur les saintes coutumes de ses pères ||</div>\n<div class=\"pp\"><span class=\"ppa\">4</span> purifié d’une faute, qui\na subi l’expiation, pur, <span class=\"aut\">Sol.</span>\n(<span class=\"aut\">And.</span> <span class=\"refch\">13, 8</span>)\n||</div>\n<div class=\"pp\"><span class=\"ppa\">5</span> <span class=\"ital\">rar.</span> <span class=\"ital\">en parl. des dieux,</span>\nsaint, vénérable, <span class=\"aut\">Orph.</span> <span class=\"oeuv\">H.</span> <span class=\"refch\">76, 2 ;</span> <span class=\"oeuv\">Arg.</span> <span class=\"refch\">27</span> ||</div>\n<div class=\"pp\"><span class=\"ppa\">6</span> <span class=\"grec\">οἱ\nὅσιοι,</span> les purs, <span class=\"ital\">n. de prêtres à\nDelphes,</span> <span class=\"aut\">Plut.</span> <span class=\"oeuv\">M.</span> <span class=\"refpa\">292</span><span class=\"refpb\">d</span>, <span class=\"refpa\">365</span><span class=\"refpb\">a</span> ||</div>\n</div>\n<div clas